      {
        "id": "text",
        "text": "We registered the protocol internally before searching and aligned every step with the PRISMA 2020 checklist. The eligibility frame was deliberately tighter than earlier reviews [33] for one reason: tropical and warm-climate buildings face a cooling-dominated thermal balance that fundamentally changes which green-wall mechanisms matter. Mixing those data with continental winter heating studies dilutes the synthesis. Two reviewers screened independently. A third reviewer adjudicated disagreements only if consensus failed after a 30-minute discussion â this happened on 23 of 812 records (2.8%). Cohen's Îº across screening rounds reached 0.78, comfortably above the 0.7 threshold often cited for systematic reviews. The risk of bias was assessed using a modified ROBINS-I tool adapted for environmental field experiments, with seven domains scored low/moderate/high."
